Relative to an orthonormal basis ${bold(e_1), bold(e_2), bold(e_3)}$, writing $bold(a) = sum_i a_i bold(e_i)$ and $bold(b) = sum_j b_j bold(e_j)$ gives
$ bold(a) dot bold(b) = a_1 b_1 + a_2 b_2 + a_3 b_3, quad abs(bold(a))^2 = a_1^2 + a_2^2 + a_3^2. $
In $RR^n$ this coordinate formula defines the dot product directly, $bold(a) dot bold(b) = sum_(i=1)^n a_i b_i$, and it satisfies $bold(e_i) dot bold(e_j) = delta_(i j)$.
